## Summary
Authored one lesson at `courses/sar-…-samolotow/lessons/tekstura-morfologia-i-change-detection-jako-feature-engineering-pod-ai.json` — module `m4`, 15 min — following `generate_lesson/SKILL.md` end-to-end. Touched no other lesson, `course.json`, or `scripts/ralph/`.
**Structure (7 sections, 3 theory + 4 widgets):**
1. **theory** — framing (CFAR mask → AI features) + GLCM contrast, with the `∑∑ P(i,j)(i-j)²` formula glossed symbol-by-symbol (intuition-first, per the audience override) + real-tile inline image
2. **code** — implement `glcm_contrast` in pure NumPy on a real Sentinel-1 crop, builds a block contrast map (live output); 4 tests incl. a known-value check (checkerboard contrast = 1.0)
3. **theory** — morphology for cleaning CFAR masks (erosion/dilation/opening/closing) + before/after figure
4. **parametricExplorer** — SE-size slider + opening/closing/both select, live on a synthesized noisy mask
5. **theory** — change detection: why **log-ratio**, not difference (multiplicative speckle), formula glossed + co-registered-pair figure
6. **plotImage** — log-ratio change map (sea ≈ 0 dB, new ship +8 dB), byte-for-byte reproducible source
7. **quiz** — difference vs. log-ratio, distractors drawn from the "dB is cosmetic" / "Gaussian-blur the speckle" misconceptions
**Assets generated** (all from the real Sentinel-1 tiles already in the course; runtime venv has only numpy/cv2/matplotlib/PIL, so no skimage/scipy dependency in learner code): 1 real cropped land tile, GLCM contrast-map reference, morphology before/after, change-detection pair, log-ratio plot.
**Verification:** `LessonSchema.safeParse` → OK · `findLessonAssetIssues` → `[]` (0 missing, 0 external URLs) · code solution passes all 4 tests while the starter correctly fails · explorer runs across all param combos · plotImage source reproduces the PNG byte-for-byte · 3 theory beats 219–303 words each, every ≥300-char theory carries a captioned inline image.
